# Environment for running Turnframe's own tests and examples locally.
#
#   cp .env.dev .env    # .env is ignored by git; put real keys only there
#
# The tests and examples/console below load the repository's .env on their own,
# so nothing needs exporting. A variable already set in the shell wins over the
# file. The library crates read no environment at all.
#
# Every variable is optional: a test whose variable is unset prints SKIPPED and
# passes.
#
# Leave a line commented out when you do not use it. An empty value is not the
# same as an unset one: an empty model or base URL is used as given, and the
# console example treats an empty key as a key.
#
# The live tests also skip whenever CI is set, so keep CI out of this file.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# examples/console: the one example that talks to a real model
#   cargo run -p console
#
# The first key found wins, in this order: OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini. With no
# key it falls back to a local Ollama.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...

# Model for whichever vendor was chosen. Defaults: gpt-4o-2024-08-06,
# claude-sonnet-4-20250514, gemini-2.0-flash, qwen3:8b (Ollama).
# TURNFRAME_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Ollama daemon, when no key is set. Default: the local daemon.
# OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Trace every turn, from the message to the reply: each model request with its
# full prompt, each response, each decision. One JSON line per event, in a new
# file per run. 1 writes into the repository's traces/, which git ignores; any
# other value names the directory. The travel desk, onboarding and mixed examples
# read it too. Traces hold what was typed, so keep them out of anything shared.
# TURNFRAME_TRACE=1

# A TOML file merged over the console's configuration: a partial file changes
# only what it states. [narration] steps = true also has each understanding step
# said in the user's language, one small model call per step.
# TURNFRAME_CONFIG=console.toml


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live provider smoke tests: one structured call and one streamed call
#   cargo test -p turnframe-provider-<name> --test live_smoke -- --nocapture
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OpenAI, Azure OpenAI or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# TURNFRAME_OPENAI_LIVE_KEY=sk-...
# TURNFRAME_OPENAI_LIVE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini                 # default: gpt-4o-mini
# TURNFRAME_OPENAI_LIVE_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1  # default: OpenAI's own

# Anthropic Messages API.
# TURNFRAME_ANTHROPIC_LIVE_KEY=sk-ant-...
# TURNFRAME_ANTHROPIC_LIVE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001  # default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# TURNFRAME_ANTHROPIC_LIVE_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com  # default: Anthropic's own

# Gemini developer API (Vertex AI is not covered by these tests).
# TURNFRAME_GEMINI_LIVE_KEY=AIza...
# TURNFRAME_GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash            # default: gemini-2.5-flash
# TURNFRAME_GEMINI_LIVE_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta  # default: Google's own
# TURNFRAME_GEMINI_LIVE_TRANSPORT=schema                  # schema (default) or function

# Ollama. The model is the switch: an ordinary daemon has no credential.
# TURNFRAME_OLLAMA_LIVE_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# TURNFRAME_OLLAMA_LIVE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434   # default: http://127.0.0.1:11434
# TURNFRAME_OLLAMA_LIVE_TOKEN=...                         # only behind an authenticating proxy

# AWS Bedrock Converse. The model id is the switch; credentials come from the
# ordinary AWS chain (environment, profile, container or instance role).
# TURNFRAME_BEDROCK_LIVE_MODEL=anthropic.claude-3-5-haiku-20241022-v1:0
# TURNFRAME_BEDROCK_LIVE_REGION=eu-central-1              # default: whatever the AWS chain resolves
# AWS_PROFILE=default
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=...


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation corpus against a real model
#   cargo test -p turnframe-eval --test live_corpus -- --nocapture
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# TURNFRAME_EVAL_LIVE_KEY=sk-...
# TURNFRAME_EVAL_LIVE_VENDOR=openai                       # openai (default), anthropic or gemini
# TURNFRAME_EVAL_LIVE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini                   # default per vendor: gpt-4o-mini,
#                                                         # claude-haiku-4-5-20251001, gemini-2.5-flash
# TURNFRAME_EVAL_LIVE_REPORT=target/eval-live-report.json # write the machine-readable report here


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL store tests
#   cargo test -p turnframe-store-postgres
#
# The suite owns the tf_* tables it creates, so never point this at a database
# you care about. CONTRIBUTING.md has the docker command for a throwaway one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# TURNFRAME_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://turnframe:turnframe@localhost:5432/turnframe_test
